  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The best configuration so far is config_044 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat, acc 0.715). The two main untested levers on top of this are fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) and aggregation (avgpool vs. transformer). From the rna_only comparison (config_002 avgpool 0.650 vs. config_007 transformer 0.653), aggregation choice appears to have negligible impact, whereas fusion strategy has been tested only as 'concat' across all multimodal runs, leaving it completely unexplored. Config_008 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while holding every other variable identical to config_044, giving a clean single-variable test of whether learned or adaptive weighting of the two modalities can improve on simple concatenation. Under a limited budget, resolving this high-uncertainty, high-impact design choice (how to combine the strong image and RNA representations) is more informative than re-testing aggregation, which prior evidence suggests is a minor factor."
}

